{"w":2400,"h":3396,"lines":[{"w":0.083333117167154969,"y":0.03514353187883501,"t":"Reading","x":0.8329071076961363,"h":0.016384960484588929,"c":1},{"h":0.017548689151400065,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","y":0.079620402700895543,"w":0.30893903096516928,"c":1,"x":0.078043886049812231},{"y":0.11570342243011378,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","c":1,"h":0.02224565872174411,"x":0.078038344750045965,"w":0.82744216918945312},{"c":1,"t":"Passage 2 below.","y":0.13515901082370174,"w":0.17078189849853515,"x":0.076131684372443359,"h":0.016003780005537038},{"w":0.75735371907552085,"y":0.17438052796519954,"t":"Climate change reveals ancient artefacts in Norway's glaciers","c":1,"h":0.023203282530372404,"x":0.11720480359892975},{"w":0.80887023925781254,"y":0.21215453909556736,"t":"A Well above the treeline in Norway's highest mountains, ancient fields of ice are shrinking","x":0.073966878265341998,"h":0.020086227794418043,"c":1},{"w":0.77792622884114593,"x":0.12132785973565272,"t":"as Earth's climate warms. As the ice has vanished, it has been giving up the treasures it has","c":1,"h":0.01846618562480451,"y":0.23085502202948327},{"x":0.12139918813710353,"y":0.24999999983980103,"c":1,"t":"preserved in cold storage for the last 6,000 years - items such as ancient arrows and skis","h":0.017441860778592888,"w":0.75925923665364592},{"c":1,"w":0.74303019205729171,"x":0.12128080434625076,"t":"from Viking Age* traders. And those artefacts have provided archaeologists with some","y":0.26532625560289591,"h":0.020804396226071886},{"w":0.58024693806966143,"y":0.28474676066706861,"x":0.12139916457142211,"t":"surprising insights into how ancient Norwegians made their livings.","c":1,"h":0.017667844522968323},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.31104651135194283,"x":0.076131687256702066,"w":0.016460905075073237,"c":1,"t":"B"},{"t":"Organic materials like textiles and hides are relatively rare finds at archaeological sites.","h":0.017515476797438589,"w":0.75102879842122405,"c":1,"y":0.31242638382091359,"x":0.11728395455052303},{"h":0.017667844522968323,"x":0.12139918088984804,"y":0.3297997645167503,"c":1,"w":0.75102879842122405,"t":"This is because unless they're protected from the microorganisms that cause decay, they"},{"c":1,"w":0.74291976928710945,"x":0.11927685103747034,"h":0.019467726753513492,"t":"tend not to last long. Extreme cold is one reliable way to keep artefacts relatively fresh","y":0.34729877549288757},{"w":0.73662551879882809,"c":1,"h":0.018895348053517669,"t":"for a few thousand years, but once thawed out, these materials experience degradation","x":0.12139917463537822,"y":0.36482558178361602},{"w":0.15226337432861325,"t":"relatively swiftly.","x":0.11934156376336302,"h":0.016022611984234936,"y":0.38368669047147375,"c":1},{"y":0.40962581585209956,"t":"With climate change shrinking ice cover around the world, glacial archaeologists need to","x":0.12128294467222152,"h":0.020210979403258778,"w":0.75742741902669264,"c":1},{"y":0.42873969430323866,"h":0.018934723906859574,"x":0.11934155395398742,"t":"race the clock to find newly revealed artefacts, preserve them, and study them. If something","w":0.78600824991861984,"c":1},{"t":"fragile dries and is windblown it might very soon be lost to science, or an arrow might","y":0.44586413964906813,"h":0.01968759979319934,"c":1,"w":0.74088892618815105,"x":0.12131746910912132},{"w":0.72645172119140622,"c":1,"h":0.019203851023607776,"t":"be exposed and then covered again by the next snow and remain well-preserved. The","x":0.1192839036694527,"y":0.46363599875799077},{"x":0.11926084876345755,"t":"unpredictability means that glacial archaeologists have to be systematic in their approach","y":0.47965135135243586,"w":0.7635612996419272,"h":0.021193948033560894,"c":1},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"to fieldwork.","x":0.11934156127303261,"c":1,"y":0.49999999985121613,"w":0.11316872914632164},{"w":0.016460905075073251,"h":0.014534883982160851,"c":1,"t":"C","x":0.074074074129130044,"y":0.52616279042171032},{"w":0.74914164225260427,"c":1,"y":0.52666064062691154,"h":0.019578787687950849,"t":"Over a nine-year period, a team of archaeologists, which included Lars Pilø of Oppland","x":0.11925560715336209},{"c":1,"x":0.1192858087169418,"t":"County Council, Norway, and James Barrett of the McDonald Institute for Archaeological","y":0.54451035234850853,"w":0.77171218872070313,"h":0.018082382260559582},{"y":0.56232874564510593,"w":0.78408426920572916,"x":0.12133045441868698,"h":0.018631457720825084,"t":"Research, surveyed patches of ice in Oppland, an area of south-central Norway that is home","c":1},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"t":"to some of the country's highest mountains. Reindeer once congregated on these icy patches","y":0.58127208486840387,"x":0.11934157026345815,"w":0.79012344360351561},{"t":"in the later summer months to escape biting insects, and from the late Stone Age**, hunters","h":0.027036564650608552,"x":0.11907038354336691,"c":1,"y":0.59386261985657585,"w":0.78650426228841153},{"c":1,"x":0.1192578595617499,"t":"followed. In addition, trade routes threaded through the mountain passes of Oppland, linking","w":0.79234980265299471,"y":0.61568124860400553,"h":0.019838690336517306},{"y":0.6307461554724515,"h":0.02315324664256313,"w":0.3813672383626302,"t":"settlements in Norway to the rest of Europe.","c":1,"x":0.1190503676598893},{"w":0.761493886311849,"x":0.11924787891944505,"c":1,"h":0.02016255206859574,"t":"The slow but steady movement of glaciers tends to destroy anything at their bases, so the","y":0.66086275516834436},{"x":0.11728396275645556,"y":0.68021201410533949,"w":0.75308639526367183,"h":0.017462404653236896,"c":1,"t":"team focused on stationary patches of ice, mostly above 1,400 metres. That ice is found"},{"w":0.75118494669596347,"y":0.69606011343262897,"c":1,"x":0.11926166268779147,"t":"amid fields of frost-weathered boulders, fallen rocks, and exposed bedrock that for nine","h":0.021336179178370496},{"h":0.016038020171040723,"c":1,"y":0.71511627891776353,"w":0.3703703816731771,"t":"months of the year is buried beneath snow.","x":0.117283944820133},{"c":1,"h":0.021025249899065623,"t":"'Fieldwork is hard work - hiking with all our equipment, often camping on permafrost -","x":0.11715026632546245,"y":0.74123735118784639,"w":0.76361343383789071},{"t":"but very rewarding. You're rescuing the archaeology, bringing the melting ice to wider","x":0.11934156964432285,"c":1,"y":0.76017441899375837,"w":0.73868311564127609,"h":0.018977524675385049},{"t":"attention, discovering a unique environmental history and really connecting with the natural","c":1,"y":0.77717207292831458,"w":0.79027119954427083,"x":0.11721268644870292,"h":0.020255470725195401},{"x":0.11728395286915468,"c":1,"y":0.79505300347228403,"t":"environment, says Barrett.","w":0.2345678965250651,"h":0.017446995904785489},{"y":0.85747938769538234,"x":0.078189289616622179,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"t":"* Viking Age: a period of European history from around 700 CE to around 1050 CE when Scandinavian Vikings migrated throughout","w":0.7921810913085936},{"t":"Europe by means of trade and warfare","h":0.010174418787512463,"y":0.87209302315944426,"w":0.23251029968261722,"x":0.088477360335885838,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"** The Stone Age: a period in early history that began about 3.4 million years ago","y":0.883680773150196,"w":0.48779632568359371,"h":0.01477591758341612,"x":0.073997801725482482},{"w":0.02880658467610675,"t":"65","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"y":0.90697674397575145,"x":0.88477366229157628},{"w":0.2544967142740886,"x":0.71941411425921253,"c":1,"h":0.029868787534104935,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","y":0.9541780374336537}]}